<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niš</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Naissus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niš is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> on the Nišava river, one of the oldest cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. As Roman Naissus it was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a>. Taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the late 14th century, it saw a Christian victory in 1443 during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a>'s Long Campaign, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> deserted the Ottoman army. Serbia gained the city in 1878.</p></div>
